  "description": "MASTUY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C333 H323 Dy21 F21 N70 O77 7+,12(H2 O1),7(Cl1 1-),12(C1 H1 Cl3),3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy13 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy14 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy15 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy16 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy17 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy18 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy19 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy20 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy21 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 7 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.740-3.842 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.17-113.83°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy21(L)7(LH)7(tfa)7]Cl7·15H2O·7MeOH·12CHCl3. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
